Mouse Bites Inc. has received intel that the Crazy Ants, our rival
concern, are planning something major.

We suspect a private equity roll-up play in the fragmented hotel
fragrances and potpourri sector in FY Q3 2026.

What we know so far:

  - Respiratory therapists at local urgent care clinics report
    clusters of new-onset reactive airway cases in residents of
    three subway-accessible facilities this year.

  - A Department of State filing cross-references institutional
    purchasing data via a RTK request to the Bucks County purchasing
    office, and matches the Crazy Ants Fragrance Compounder
    Subsidiary SDS sheets (obtained through an OSHA 300 log FOIA on
    the contract facility) against the Protected Substances List.

  - "SAME ARTISAN QUALITY, NEW OWNERSHIP" signs are popping up at
    mom-and-pop crafters and aging Yankee Candle mall kiosks across
    Mischief City.

Right now we can see the shape. We need the blueprint. That's where
you come in, Sniffer Cadet. We need to cripple the Ants' deck before
they start yoking investors.

Your first assignment: scan the Crazy Ants network with nmap and
find the back-office host that's accidentally exposed to the
outside -- the one wired into their fragrance compounding subsidiary.

